        {
          "id": 503172088,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> This depends on a commit that was never back ported to master-3.2. Question is should it.\n\nI backported it in !1957 because it just added some #defines for ARPHRD) values (and fixed typoes in a few - ARPHRD_HW_EXP1, ARPHRD_HFI, and ARPHRD_HW_EXP2), and adds them to the value_string table for ARP hardware types.\n\nThis change itself was backported in !1958 (which comes after !1957, so the pipeline succeeded), so this one can be closed.",
